    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d611">

                <pb facs="0745" n="646" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg646"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 Bowers, Claude G/75: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Straus</hi>)<anchor n="64"
                        xml:id="d611-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-07-26T20:00:00-04:00">July 26, 1936—8 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>256. Your 660, July 26, 9 p.m I have talked with Schoelkopf<anchor n="65"
                        xml:id="d611-f2"/> at St. Jean de Luz, this evening and told him that
                    Ambassador Bowers has my authorization to leave Fuenterrabia for France or
                    elsewhere and should not remain on endangering himself and family.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d611-f1" n="64" type="source" xml:id="d611-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Oklahoma</hi> and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Cayuga</hi> for their information.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d611-f2" n="65" xml:id="d611-f2-content">
                <p>Walter H. Schoelkopf, First Secretary of Embassy in Spain.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
